  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To subtract $5.5$ from $-6.5,$ we break up $5.5$ into its whole number part ($5$) and its decimal part ($0.5$) and proceed in two steps.\n\n- We start at $-6.5$ on the number line and move $5$ places to the left, which brings us to $-11.5.$\n\n- Then, we move the remaining $0.5$ places to the left, leaving us at $-12.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14149078/assets/39ff813739eb7d023ee7949f63681a6cb7f31c3cc787550b3ed6bc6faed5084f.png)\n\nWe get $-6.5-5.5=-12.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
